data: {"seq":423,"ts":"2026-08-28T08:50:05.034Z","text":"This is the minidlna upnphttp request parser (sub_40D1FC). Notable: the chunked encoding handling at the part started with `if ( *(_DWORD *)(a1 + 116) & 0x100 )`. It parses chunked transfer: reads length via strtol, then copies chunk into dest with memmove(dest, src, len) without bounds check against the destination buffer size. a1+32 is the request buffer. This could be a heap/stack overflow.\n\nBut this is quite involved. Also GET paths route to SendResp_* handlers that serv","stream":true,"block":0}

event: thinking
data: {"seq":424,"ts":"2026-08-28T08:50:05.535Z","text":"This is the minidlna upnphttp request parser (sub_40D1FC). Notable: the chunked encoding handling at the part started with `if ( *(_DWORD *)(a1 + 116) & 0x100 )`. It parses chunked transfer: reads length via strtol, then copies chunk into dest with memmove(dest, src, len) without bounds check against the destination buffer size. a1+32 is the request buffer. This could be a heap/stack overflow.\n\nBut this is quite involved. Also GET paths route to SendResp_* handlers that serve files based on /MediaItems/<id> etc. The v8 url is parsed into v11[500] (the url) in SendResp_thumbnail/dlnafile. Path traversal possible in file serving.\n\nHowever, minidlnad doesn't run in qemu (no IP). So I can't dynamically verify.\n\nGiven the extensive environmental dead-ends, let me reconsider the s","stream":true,"block":0}

